# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: probe-ps1-done-check-misreads-utf16-report — Windows probe scripts flag complete runs INCOMPLETE
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-probe-script-defects
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

Every Windows run of intersectwith-probe (jobs 17029587294, 17029587295,
17029587296, 2026-10-08) ended its report with

: IWPROBE-INCOMPLETE  the probe did not reach its end

right after the =IWPROBE-DONE= line it claims is missing.

* Cause

The scripts write the report header with =Set-Content -Encoding utf8=
(UTF-8 BOM), then append with =Tee-Object -FilePath -Append=, which in
Windows PowerShell 5 writes UTF-16LE. The file is mixed (UTF-8 BOM + CRLF,
then UTF-16LE without BOM), and =Select-String -Path $report -Pattern
'^...-DONE'= reads it as UTF-8 and never matches.

* Resolution so far

run-intersectwith-probe.ps1 (clautolisp 2.3.10) decides on the captured
lines instead of re-reading the file. The same check is still in
run-getcname-probe.ps1, run-optkw-probe.ps1, run-path-sysvars-probe.ps1 and
run-pgp-probe.ps1 (=grep -l "Select-String -Path" scripts/*.ps1=).

* Proposal

Apply the same change to those four; better, write the report in ONE
encoding (=Out-File -Encoding utf8 -Append=, or collect and Set-Content
once), so the artefacts no longer need byte-level decoding.

* Fix (2026-10-22)

Took the "one encoding" route, the pattern already in
run-real-transport-probe.ps1, run-block-comment-probe.ps1,
run-curve-geometry-probe.ps1, run-request-locals-probe.ps1 and
run-console-flood-probe.ps1: the report is created with
=Set-Content -Encoding utf8= and EVERY later write is
=Add-Content -Encoding utf8= (=ForEach-Object { $_; Add-Content ... }= where
the line is also echoed to the job log). No =Tee-Object= is left on a report
in scripts/run-*.ps1, so the final =Select-String -Path $report= DONE check
reads a UTF-8 file. Changed:

- run-getcname-probe.ps1, run-pgp-probe.ps1, run-path-sysvars-probe.ps1:
  the four scripts named above (DONE check via Select-String -Path, kept);
- run-intersectwith-probe.ps1, run-optkw-probe.ps1: already decided on the
  captured lines (kept), but their reports were still mixed UTF-8/UTF-16;
- run-pathname-probe.ps1, run-encoding-experiment.ps1,
  run-lispsys-bom-probe.ps1: no DONE check, same mixed reports.

run-vendor-probes.ps1 still uses =Tee-Object -FilePath $log= (no -Append):
that writes the whole log in ONE encoding (UTF-16 with a BOM), which
Get-Content and compare-observations.py read back, so it is not this bug and
was left alone.

No PowerShell on the Linux box: the edits were reviewed by reading them.
Closes when the next Windows CAD run of these probes shows complete reports
(the DONE line present and no spurious *-INCOMPLETE line) in UTF-8 artefacts.
